Backport the cgroup v2 freezer to the prepared LineageOS 4.9.337 kernel.

Implementation source: Linux 5.10.272
  https://github.com/gregkh/linux/commit/aca95a35f1bcc0626c4fa4d1252bf2d4c990a1a2
Original feature (Roman Gushchin / Tejun Heo, Linux 5.2):
  https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/76f969e8948d82e78e1bc4beb6b9465908e74873
Prerequisite: sched/core set_special_state(), adapted from
  https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/b5bf9a90bbebffba888c9144c5a8a10317b04064
License: GPL-2.0

Keep the 4.9 monolithic cgroup core, private locks, task iterator API and
signal types. Add exact css_set task counts and live-descendant counts;
cover creation, migration, fork, vfork, exit, ptrace and SIGSTOP/SIGKILL.
The 4.9 fork return path has no calculate_sigpending(), so explicitly mark
new children with TIF_SIGPENDING when assigning the freezer jobctl trap.
Use the existing 4.9 task-work notification mechanism; do not add the 5.10
TIF_NOTIFY_SIGNAL path or the optional cgroup freezer trace events.

ReKernel detects the backported jobctl feature instead of the numeric
kernel version. The v1 freezer and WALT remain available. This patch does
not implement Android binder freezer ioctls or change ROM task profiles.
Apply after ReKernel and all three Mihomo patches.

Serialize STOPPED/TRACED/DEAD transitions against concurrent wakeups using
pi_lock, retaining 4.9 debug state tracking and the WALT scheduler.
